    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0464" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1935</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3281. Your instruction 1758, October 12, and cablegram 2452, November 13.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office inform me that British Government agree for the present not to
                    interfere with cargoes of tobacco shipped to neutral consignees in neutral
                    countries and state that in these circumstances tobacco in all its forms
                    destined for Holland will no longer be required to be consigned to Netherlands
                    Oversea Trust.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
